   \[
   3 - 1 + 1 = 3 \text{ days}
   \]

#### Step 3: Total Days in One Year
Now, we can sum the days calculated:
\[
\text{Total days in one year} = 5 \text{ (July)} + 31 \text{ (August)} + 3 \text{ (September)} = 39 \text{ days}
\]

#### Step 4: Total Days Over the Years
Since the number of cake-eating days is the same for each of the 9 years, we multiply the number of days by the number of years:
\[
\text{Total cake-eating days} = 39 \text{ days/year} \times 9 \text{ years} = 351 \text{ days}
\]

### Final Answer
The total number of cake-eating days observed by the end of 2016 is:
\[
\boxed{351}
\]

