   \]
   where \(a\) and \(b\) are the lengths of the legs, and \(c\) is the length of the hypotenuse. In this case, we will let one leg be \(9\) meters, and the other leg be \(x\) meters, where \(x\) is a consecutive integer. The hypotenuse will then be \(x + 1\) meters (the next consecutive integer).

