\[
x = 3m \quad \text{and} \quad y = 3n
\]
where \( m \) and \( n \) are coprime integers (i.e., \( \text{gcd}(m, n) = 1 \)).

The lcm can then be expressed as:
\[
\text{lcm}(x, y) = \frac{x \cdot y}{\text{gcd}(x, y)} = \frac{(3m)(3n)}{3} = 3mn
\]

The condition that the lcm is twelve times one of the integers gives us two cases to consider:
1. \( 3mn = 12x = 12(3m) \) leading to \( mn = 12m \)
2. \( 3mn = 12y = 12(3n) \) leading to \( mn = 12n \)

