The product of the positive divisors of a number \( n \) can be calculated using the formula:
\[
P(n) = n^{t(n)/2}
\]
where \( t(n) \) is the number of positive divisors of \( n \).

We need to set this equal to \( n^6 \):
\[
n^{t(n)/2} = n^6
\]

