🔄 开始测试问题: On a true-false test of 100 items, every question that is a multiple of 4 is true, and all others are false. If a student marks every item that is a multiple of 3 false and all others true, how many of the 100 items will be correctly answered?

2025-07-13 08:54:15 - INFO - ```python
def solve():
    total_questions = 100
    true_answers = set()
    false_answers = set()

    # Mark every question that is a multiple of 4 as true
    for i in range(1, total_questions + 1):
        if i % 4 == 0:
            true_answers.add(i)
        else:
            false_answers.add(i)

    # Student marks every item that is a multiple of 3 as false
    student_answers = set()
    for i in range(1, total_questions + 1):
        if i % 3 == 0:
            student_answers.add(i)  # Student marks false
        else:
            student_answers.add(i)  # Student marks true

    # Calculate correct answers
    correct_answers = true_answers.intersection(student_answers)
    correct_count = len(correct_answers)

    return correct_count

# Call the solve function and print the result
result = solve()
print(result)
```
