To solve the congruence \( 64x \equiv 2 \pmod{66} \), we can follow these steps:

1. Simplify the congruence.
2. Find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of the coefficient of \( x \) and the modulus.
3. Check if the gcd divides the constant term on the right side of the congruence.
