\sqrt{k^2 \cdot 10} = \sqrt{29}
\]
Squaring both sides:
\[
10k^2 = 29 \implies k^2 = \frac{29}{10} \implies k = \sqrt{\frac{29}{10}} = \frac{\sqrt{29}}{\sqrt{10}}
