### Step 3: Calculate \( \text{lcm}(1, 2, \ldots, 25) \)
The LCM of a set of integers is found by taking the highest power of each prime number that appears in the factorization of any of the integers in the set.

The prime factorization of the integers from 1 to 25 includes the following primes and their highest powers:

- \( 2^4 \) (from \( 16 \))
