    # cos(arccos(2x)) = 2x
    # cos(arccos(3x)) = 3x
    # We can express the equation in terms of y = cos(theta)
    
    # We will use the identity cos(a + b + c) = cos(a)cos(b)cos(c) - sin(a)sin(b)sin(c)
    # where a = arccos(x), b = arccos(2x), c = arccos(3x)
    
    # We can derive the polynomial by substituting and simplifying
