k & -1 & -1 \\
1 & 1 & -k
\end{pmatrix}
\]

### Step 4: Calculating the Determinant
To find the values of \( k \) for which the determinant of \( A \) is zero, we compute \( \det(A) \):

\[
\det(A) = \begin{vmatrix}
1 & k & -1 \\
k & -1 & -1 \\
1 & 1 & -k
\end{vmatrix}
\]

