We start by simplifying the right-hand side of the equation. We can use the identity for tangent in terms of sine and cosine:

\[
\tan \theta = \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta}.
\]

To express \( \frac{\cos 50^{\circ}}{1 - \sin 50^{\circ}} \) in terms of tangent, we can multiply the numerator and denominator by \( 1 + \sin 50^{\circ} \):

\[
