To find the volume, we need to compute the scalar triple product \(|\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})|\). The formula for the volume of the tetrahedron can be expressed in terms of the angles between the vectors. The scalar triple product can be calculated using the cosine of the angles between the vectors.

