\]

This indicates that the maximum value of \(w_y\) achieved in this specific case is \(0.5\).

### Final Answer
Thus, the largest possible value of \((\mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v}) \cdot \mathbf{w}\) is 

\[
\boxed{0.5}.
