   \[
   \text{Ways to Form Pair} = 13 \times 6 \times 12 \times 4 = 3744
   \]

3. Calculate the probability of forming a pair:
   \[
   \text{Probability of Pair} = \frac{\text{Ways to Form Pair}}{\text{Total Ways}} = \frac{3744}{22100}
