   \[
   \left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^n \leq \frac{1}{4}
   \]
   To solve for \( n \), we can take the logarithm of both sides. Using the natural logarithm, we have:
   \[
   \ln\left(\left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^n\right) \leq \ln\left(\frac{1}{4}\right)
   \]
   This simplifies to:
   \[
